Actually, in pre-1979 Loglan, lujvo were made precisely by such unsystematic
shortening, and people found that they couldn't learn the words.  So the
unsystematic technique WAS in use first, and the earlier version of Loglan
suffered the consequences of having to reinvent the word-making system.  This
led to many people dropping out, and the start of the political squabble that
eventually resulted in the split between TLI Loglan and our version.

